  "teach": {
    "narration_en": "ال means 'the'. With most letters — the 'moon letters' — you say the ل clearly: القَمَرْ, al-qamar, the moon. But with 14 'sun letters' the ل goes silent and the next letter doubles instead: الشَّمْسْ is said ash-shams, the sun — written with a ل you never hear. The two names are the example: قَمَر keeps its ل, شَمْس swallows it.",
